# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in your own values. Never commit real keys.
# Each teammate needs their own .env.local. Restart `npm run dev` after editing it.
#
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY (optional)
#   Google Map Tiles API key for Photorealistic 3D Tiles. When missing or invalid the app falls
#   back to an OpenStreetMap raster globe and shows a banner; everything else still works.
#   Google tiles are used for DISPLAY ONLY. They are never a data source for the simulation.
#
#   How to get one:
#     1. Google Cloud Console -> create or pick a project with billing enabled.
#     2. APIs & Services -> Library -> enable "Map Tiles API".
#     3. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key.
#     4. Restrict the key (Edit key):
#          Application restrictions: Websites -> add  localhost:*  and your deploy domain.
#          API restrictions: Restrict key -> Map Tiles API only.
#     5. Billing -> Budgets & alerts -> set a small monthly budget with email alerts.
#   See README.md "Google 3D tiles setup".
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
#
# VITE_FIRMS_MAP_KEY (optional)
#   NASA FIRMS map key for the "Live fires" tab (near-real-time satellite fire detections).
#   Without it the tab shows how to get a key and nothing is fetched; the simulator is unaffected.
#   Free, no billing: https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/ (sent by email, 32 hex chars).
#   Limit: 5000 transactions per 10 minutes per key; a world query costs tens, and the app caches
#   results for 10 minutes. Like the Google key it is compiled into the public bundle, so every
#   visitor of a deployment shares its budget. Never commit it; never paste it in chat or issues.
VITE_FIRMS_MAP_KEY=
